            <div type="transcription" xml:lang="pal">
                <ab xml:id="MP1027_trc-p1">
                    <lb n="1" xml:id="trc-p1-l1"/>A māh Day abar sāl 103 ī pas az ōy bay Yazdgird
                    šāhān šāh ī nah ī ōy bay Xusrō ī Ōhrmazdān ud rōz Rašn ka <persName ref="people:Tab017">Wanandpanāh</persName> kē tasūg ī
                        <lb n="2" xml:id="trc-p1-l2"/>Dēl ī Dēlān ī abar Taburestān dādestān čiyōnīh
                    tasūg ī <unclear>Sūrīgān</unclear> ī abar Taburestān dādestān pad dehīhā(!)
                    pad-iš framān sāxtan pad dehīhā pūdag ham tasūg ī <lb n="3" xml:id="trc-p1-l3"/>Dēl ī Dēlān būd B mardān ī Bōxt nām ō <persName ref="people:Tab017">Wanandpanāh</persName> guft kū mardān ī Frawardīn
                    nām būd mardān ī Ātaxšbōyag nām būd kardērīh pus wispān ham tasūg ī Dēl ī Dēlān
                    az <lb n="4" xml:id="trc-p1-l4"/><supplied>ān</supplied>
                    <unclear><placeName>Haspīn-raz</placeName></unclear> deh būd hēnd ud mardān ī <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> nām
                    Dēlānfarrox pus mardān ī <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> nām mardān ī <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> nām Zādānfarrox
                    pus mardān ī <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> nām Farrox-Xusrō <lb n="5" xml:id="trc-p1-l5"/>pus
                    az ān <unclear>Haspīn-raz</unclear> deh <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> ōy Frawardīn duxt
                    Rašnweh ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> ōy Ātaxšbōyag pusarāwandān
                    ud xwāstagdārān B1 ud pad bun ī ān <unclear>Haspīn-raz</unclear>
                    <lb n="6" xml:id="trc-p1-l6"/>deh kišwzār zamīg ī kōfag xār-wanīgān xwānēnd
                    g(rīw) I āhang kē az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ​​​ī mardān ī Yazdgird nām
                    būd ud any mard ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ​​ī <lb n="7" xml:id="trc-p1-l7"/>mardān ī Zādānfarrox nām būd ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī
                    [xwāstag-paymāyagān-ī] Māhōy nām būd ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī
                    mardān ī Māhanōš(?) nām būd sāmān | B2 ud zamīg ī [kōfag] ǰadārīh xwānēnd <lb n="8" xml:id="trc-p1-l8"/>g(rīw) 2 āhang kē az ēw zayt ī zand ud az ēw zayt
                    ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī Dērā nām būd ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī
                    mardān ī Farroxzād nām būd <lb n="9" xml:id="trc-p1-l9"/>ud az ēw zayt Ï zamīg ī
                    xwāstagdārān ī ōy Māh-ōš ud any mard sāmān | B3 ud zamīg ī kōfag wanīgarīh xwand
                    g(rīw) I āhang kē az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī Farroxān nām ud az ēw zayt ī <lb n="10" xml:id="trc-p1-l10"/>zamīg ī mardān ī Farroxgušnasp nām ud az ēw zayt
                    ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī ōy Dērā ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī ham <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName>
                    sāmān | B4 zamīg ī <lb n="11" xml:id="trc-p1-l11"/>ī kōfag g(rīw) I k(abīz) 8
                    āhang kē az ēw zayt ī zamīg ud xānag ī xwastagdārān ī mardān ī Yazdōy nām būd ud
                    any mard ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ud xānag ī xwāstagdārān ī mardān ī ōy Dēra <lb n="12" xml:id="trc-p1-l12"/>ud any mard ud az dō zayt ī čand ud rawišn ī
                    zamānag drahm ī az ān <unclear>Haspīn-raz</unclear> deh sāmān | B5 ud xānag ud
                    spinǰānagīh ud tis enyā abar <supplied>nimāyēd ud</supplied> wizandag kard rāy
                    zyān ēwēn sē ǰādag az 6 <lb n="13" xml:id="trc-p1-l13"/>bārag-bār ud ham tasūg ī
                    Dēl ī Dēlān pad bun ī Frōd deh razists zamīg ī kōfag g(rīw) l k(abīz) 5 āhang kē
                    az ēw zayt ī razist zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī mardān ī Wahištān nām <lb n="14" xml:id="trc-p1-l14"/>būd ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī mardān ī ōy
                    Ātaxšbōyag ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī az ān Frōd deh ud az ēw zayt ī
                    pēš sāmān | B6 ud raz ud sarw ud tis enyā <lb n="15" xml:id="trc-p1-l15"/>abar
                    nimāyēd ud ēd kard rāy zyān ēwēn sē ǰadag az sē bār dō bār ud kišwānzār zamīg ī
                    kōfag ī ān-iz pad bun ī ān <unclear>Haspīn-raz</unclear> deh ud mayg-rist
                    xwānēnd g(rīw) 3 āhang kē az zayt ī <lb n="16" xml:id="trc-p1-l16"/>rēš ud az
                        <supplied>ēw</supplied> zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī Wahmandān nām xwāstagdārān ī
                    mardān ī Wahmanpanāh nām būd ud az dō zayt ī zamīg ī Anagrān sāmān | B7 ud zamīg
                    ī kōfag asp-tāzān xwānēnd g(rīw) āhang kē az ēw <lb n="17" xml:id="trc-p1-l17"/>zayt ī rēš ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī mardān ī Ērāzād nām būd ud
                    az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī Āzādxusrō nām {ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī
                    Āzādxusrō nām sāmān} | B8 ud zamīg <lb n="18" xml:id="trc-p1-l18"/>ī [kōfag]
                    damēnag ul-(ā)mad ī kišw ī g(rīw) l āhang kē az ēw zayt ī škihist ud az ēw zayt
                    ī zamīg ī xwāstagdārān ī ōy Dēlānfarrox ud az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī Anagrān ud az ēw
                    zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī <lb n="19" xml:id="trc-p1-l19"/>Dābōy nām ud any mard
                    sāmān | B9 ud zamīg ī kōfag hurām xwānēnd zayt g(rīw) 6 āhang kē az dō zayt ī
                    zamīg ī mardān ī Dābōy nām ud any mard uz az ēw zayt ī zamīg ī mardān ī
                        <unclear>Wangird</unclear> nām ud az ēw zayt ī <lb n="20" xml:id="trc-p1-l20"/>zamīg ī mardān ī Frawardīndād nām sāmān | Bfinal ud
                    xānag ud spinǰānagīh ud kunǰid ud sarw ud tis enyā abar nimāyēd ud gannāg kard
                    rāy zyān ēwēn ōy Frawardīn xwēš ǰadag ud tan ī Frawardīn <lb n="21" xml:id="trc-p1-l21"/>ēwēn pad ān Frawardīn saxt kard rāy Frawardīn pad
                    paymān ī Frawardīn kard dastwarīh ō xwēšīh ud dārišn ī <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> madan
                    <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> <lb n="22" xml:id="trc-p1-l22"/>ōy
                    xwāstag nē būd čē abāg <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> guftan abar pahikārdan nē tis rāst ud ka
                    ēd xīr ōwōn čiyōn man guft būd ēstād <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> <lb n="23" xml:id="trc-p1-l23"/>ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> ōy xwāstag kē tō sāmān pad nāmagīhā ud ō
                    xwēšīh ud dārišn ī <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> madan guft nē az im rōz Rašn frāz pad tis-iz
                    ēwēnag abar ud abāg <lb n="24" xml:id="trc-p1-l24"/><persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> ud
                    <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> āgenēn ōwōn čiyōn nē pahikārdan harw
                    kē pad dastwarīh ī Windādōhrmadzd ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> āgenēn <lb n="25" xml:id="trc-p1-l25"/>ud tasūg-iz ǰud pahikafēd az <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> abēzār ud
                    <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> pad ān xīr arz 101 abāyistan ud agar tis-iz ǰuttar kunēd arz 202
                    drahm ō <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> <lb n="26" xml:id="trc-p1-l26"/>dād ud grawagān kē abāg
                    <persName ref="people:Tab019">Farrox-Xusrōyān</persName> paymān kard kū amā rāst handāxt rāst frēzān ī tō kāstan tis pad
                    ān ēwēnag čē rāy pahikārd paymān kardan nē kōxšīd <lb n="27" xml:id="trc-p1-l27"/>ud rāst wizārišnīh ī amā ān čē az paymān kard nē āmad nē ēwar nē paččēn ham ud
                    Windādōhrmad ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> āgenēn ud ēd az ham az ērmānīh ī <lb n="28" xml:id="trc-p1-l28"/>man pad-iz muhr ī tō wizīr āwišt ud pēš tō
                    azi-šān pad dīd čiyōn zaytēn wizīr ī l nīd <pc function="section">○</pc> ud
                    ān-iz <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> ī <unclear>Bōxt</unclear> guft
                    pēš <persName ref="people:Tab017">Wanandpanāh</persName> <lb n="29" xml:id="trc-p1-l29"/>būd ud
                        padist<supplied>ād</supplied>
                    <pc function="section">○</pc> ud <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> guft
                    kū im rōz Rašn amā ōwōn čiyōn Bōwt guft paymān kard ud ǰadišnīg-iz ān čē Bōxt
                    guft <lb n="30" xml:id="trc-p1-l30"/>ōwōn čiyōn Bōxt pattūg ast <pc function="section">○</pc> ud abar ēn nāmag didom sāxt ēstād čihrān ī ayārīh
                    ī tō ud nibišt <pc function="section">○</pc> ud ēn nāmag pad muhr ī ham tasūg ī
                        <lb n="31" xml:id="trc-p1-l31"/>Dēl ī Dēlān čiyōnīh ham tasūg ī
                        <unclear>Sūrīgān</unclear> pad dehīhā pad-iš framān sāxtan deh pad kārframān
                    zāyistan ud <persName ref="people:Tab017">Wanandpanāh</persName> <lb n="32" xml:id="trc-p1-l32"/>ud Dērzamān ī dibīr ud
                    muhr ī dehbedān kē kard ud az mardān ī Dād-Burz-Mihr nām Mihrpanāh pus mardān ī
                    <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> nām Yazdpanāh <lb n="33" xml:id="trc-p1-l33"/>pus az ān
                        <unclear>Haspīn-raz</unclear> deh ud abar ēwāzīh guft ud <persName ref="people:Tab015">Windādōhrmazd</persName> ud
                    <persName ref="people:Tab016">Windādyazd</persName> [ud <persName ref="people:Tab017">Wanandpanāh</persName>] ud <persName ref="people:Tab018">Yazdfarrox</persName> āwišt <pc function="section">○○</pc>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                <ab xml:id="MP1027_trans-p1">
                    <lb n="1" xml:id="trans-p1-l1"/>A Month Day (10th month) in the year 103 after
                    the late Lord Yazdgird, King of Kings, grandson of the late Lord Xusrō, son of
                    Ōhrmazd, and day Rašn (18th day), when Wanandpanāh who presided over the Law in
                    the district of <lb n="2" xml:id="trans-p1-l2"/>Dēl ī Dēlān in Taburestān and
                    likewise in the “Syrian quarter” in Taburestān in the villages (and) therefore
                    was in charge to prepare orders relating to rotten (crops) in the villages of
                        <lb n="3" xml:id="trans-p1-l3"/>Dēl ī Dēlān. B The people of Bōxt by name to
                    Wanandpanāh spoke this: &gt;&gt;The people who belong to Frawardīn by name (and) the
                    people who belong to Ātaxšbōyag by name, all (of them of) authoritative progeny,
                    (of) the same tasūg of Dēl ī Dēlān from <lb n="4" xml:id="trans-p1-l4"/><supplied>the</supplied> village of *Haspīn-raz were present and the
                    people of Yazdfarrox by name, son of Dēlānfarrox, the people of Windādyazd by
                    name, the people of Windādōhrmazd by name, son of Zādānfarrox, the people of
                    Farrox-Xusrōyān by name, son of Farrox-Xusrōy, <lb n="5" xml:id="trans-p1-l5"/>from the village of *Haspīn-raz, the sons of Farrox-Xusrōy, Rašnweh, daughter
                    of the late Frawardīn and Windādyazd and Windādōhrmazd and Yazdfarrox, the sons
                    and heirs of the late Ātaxšbōyag B1 And disposal (line 7) of a field land on a
                    slope in charge of the bun of the *Haspīn-raz <lb n="6" xml:id="trans-p1-l6"/>village—“Thorn Groves” they call it—crops of 1 grīw which (are) from one olive
                    tree of the land which belonged to the heirs of the people of Yazdgird by name
                    and another man and from one olive tree of the land which belonged to the heirs
                    of <lb n="7" xml:id="trans-p1-l7"/>the people of Zādānfarrox by name and from
                    one olive tree of the land which belonged to [the valuers of the property] of
                    Māhōy by name and from one olive tree of the land which belonged to the heirs of
                    the people of the late Māhanōš(?) by name and another man. B2 And disposal (line
                    9) of land [on a slope]—they call (it) “Maintenance”— <lb n="8" xml:id="trans-p1-l8"/>with crops of 2 which (are) from one olive tree of the
                    community and from one olive tree which belongs to the lands of the heirs of
                    Dērā by name and from one olive tree of the land which belongs to the heirs of
                    the people of Farroxzād by name, <lb n="9" xml:id="trans-p1-l9"/>and from one
                    olive tree of the land of the heirs of the late Māh-ōš and another man. B3 And
                    disposal (line 10) of crops of 1 grīw from land on a slope they call (it)
                    “Waste” which come from one olive tree of the land of the people of Farroxān by
                    name and from one olive tree of <lb n="10" xml:id="trans-p1-l10"/>the land of
                    the people of Farroxgušnasp by name and from one olive tree of the land of the
                    heirs of the late Dērā and from one olive-tree of the land of the above
                    Farrox-Xusrōyān. B4 Disposal of crops from land <lb n="11" xml:id="trans-p1-l11"/>on a slope of 1 grīw 8 kabīz which (comes) from one olive tree of land and
                    house which belong to the heirs of the people of Yazdōy by name and another man
                    and from one olive tree of land and house which belong to the heirs of the late
                    Dērā <lb n="12" xml:id="trans-p1-l12"/>and another man, and from two olive trees
                    according to the current value from the village of *Haspīn-raz. B5 And the costs
                    of house and hospitality facilities and other matters you shall take in
                    consideration and because of the damage due to the earthquake only one third
                    from 6 <lb n="13" xml:id="trans-p1-l13"/>mount loads. And (in) the same quarter
                    of Dēl ī Dēlān (which is) in charge of the bun of the “Lower Village”, forested
                    land on a slope with olives 1 grīw 5 kabīz: these (were) from one olive tree of
                    forested land which belong to the heirs of the people of Wahištān by name, <lb n="14" xml:id="trans-p1-l14"/>and from one olive-tree of the land of the
                    heirs of the late Ātaxšbōyag, and from one olive tree of the land of their heirs
                    which (is) from the “Lower village”, and from one olive tree which (is) before
                    (the latter one). B6 And disposal of vines and cypresses and other things <lb n="15" xml:id="trans-p1-l15"/>you shall take into consideration and because
                    of this event a loss of one third of the norm instead of 3 loads only 2 loads
                    and a field, an acre on a slope which also belongs to the bun of the community
                    of *Haspīn-raz—they call it “Dead as a Locust”—a crop of 3 grīw which (comes)
                    from a <lb n="16" xml:id="trans-p1-l16"/>damaged olive tree and from (an) olive
                    tree of the land which belongs to the people of Wahmandād, heir of the men of
                    Wahmanpanāh by name, and from 2 olive trees of the land of Anagrān. B7 And
                    disposal of land of a slope—“Horse Paddock” they call it—the crop of 4 grīw:
                    these (are) the following: from one <lb n="17" xml:id="trans-p1-l17"/>damaged
                    olive tree and from one olive tree of the land which belongs to the heirs of the
                    people of Ērāzād by name and from one olive tree of the land of the people of
                    Āzādxusrō by name {and from one olive tree of the people of Āzādxusrō by name}.
                    B8 And disposal of land [of a slope] <lb n="18" xml:id="trans-p1-l18"/>in a fan
                    (with wind) coming up tillage of 1 grīw: these are the following: from one
                    broken olive tree and from one olive tree of the people of <lb n="19" xml:id="trans-p1-l19"/>Dābōy by name and another man. B9 And disposal (line
                    20) of a land of a slope—“the Blissful one” they call it—with a crop of olives:
                    5 grīw: these (are) the following: from two olive trees of the land of the
                    people of Dābōy and another man, and from one olive tree of the people of
                    *Wangird and from one olive tree of <lb n="20" xml:id="trans-p1-l20"/>the land
                    of the people of Frawardīndād by name. B10 The house and the hospitality
                    (facilities) and the sesame and the cypresses and something else are involved
                    and because of the damage (by that) evil event the late Frawardīn’s own share
                    and body of Frawardīn <lb n="21-22" xml:id="trans-p1-l21-22"/> for that
                    Frawardīn because of that severe event Frawardīn made an agreement that the
                    right (of disposal) should pass to the property and maintenance of
                    Farrox-Xusrōyān (but) should not be in the right (of disposal) of Windādōhrmazd
                    and Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox, for it (is) by no means proper to proceed against
                    Farrox-Xusrōyān (and) to submit it. And if this matter (is) such as I have
                    explained that property (line 23) of Windādōhrmazd and Windādyazd <lb n="23" xml:id="trans-p1-l23"/>and Yazdfarrox of which you said that the disposal
                    (is) in the books and should suffice for the property and maintenance of
                    Farrox-Xusrōyān, not from this day Rašn onwards also about (other) things about.
                    And Against <lb n="24" xml:id="trans-p1-l24"/>Farrox-Xusrōyān and Windādōhrmazd
                    and Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox jointedly there will be no litigating. Every
                    person who claims (pahikafēd, line 25) the auctorship of Windādōhrmazd and
                    Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox jointly <lb n="25" xml:id="trans-p1-l25"/>and also in
                    another district (is) without means against Farrox-Xusrōyān and he owes 101
                    drahms to Farrox-Xusrōyān for this matter and if he acts somehow otherwise he
                    (is obliged) to give (dād, line 26) 202 drahms to Farrox-Xusrōyān. <lb n="26" xml:id="trans-p1-l26"/>And (regarding) the mortgage of the usufruct for
                    which they made an agreement with Farrox-Xusrōyān, thus: we allotted it equally.
                    We did not strive to make a contract to diminish your equal dues by that manner
                    of litigating. <lb n="27" xml:id="trans-p1-l27"/>And our equal payment is that
                    which did not come from the agreement made (is) neither assured nor a copy. Also
                    Windādōhrmazd and Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox jointly and together with my
                    humbleness <lb n="28" xml:id="trans-p1-l28"/>even with your seal they sealed the
                    document and in Your presence from them under inspection they married out one
                    “olive decision”. — And exactly that which Bōxt said Windādōhrmazd and
                    Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox before Wanandpanāh <lb n="29" xml:id="trans-p1-l29"/>confirmed and promised. — And Windādōhrmazd and Windādyazd and Yazdfarrox
                    said: this day Rašn we, as Bōxt has spoken, made the contract and also on
                    imponderabilities which Bōxt mentioned. <lb n="30" xml:id="trans-p1-l30"/>are,
                    as Bōxt (said), permanent – And from this letter he established a second (one),
                    in the same form with Your assistance, and wrote (it down), — Bz And he sealed
                    (line 33) this letter with the seal of the same district of <lb n="31" xml:id="trans-p1-l31"/>Dēl ī Dēlān likewise of the Syrian quarter to prepare
                    an order concerning the villages (and) to investigate (them) by the overseer and
                    Wanandpanāh <lb n="32" xml:id="trans-p1-l32"/>and Dērzamān the scribe and by the
                    seals of the landlords who made (the contract) and from the people of
                    Dād-Burz-Mihr by name, son of Mihrpanāh, the people of Yazdānfarrox by name, son
                    of Yazdpanāh <lb n="33" xml:id="trans-p1-l33"/>from the village of *Haspīn-raz
                    and declared (consent) unanimously, and Windādōhrmazd and Windādyazd [and
                    Wanandpanāh] and Yazdfarrox sealed it. </ab>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
</TEI>